.TH EUCLID-CLI-EKV-CREATE-TABLE 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.73" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ekv-create-table \- create a key/value table
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ekv create-table
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I TABLE
.BR \-\-partition\-key | \-p
.I ATTRIBUTE
[\fB\-\-partition\-key\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-key\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIATTRIBUTE\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-key\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a table and fixes what its items are keyed on. Both are
decisions for the life of the table: there is no altering a key
afterwards, and no adding a sort key to a table that was made without
one \- the items would have nowhere to put it.
.PP
Every item written to the table has to carry the partition key
attribute, and the sort key attribute if one is declared, each with the
declared type. An item that does not is refused.
.PP
The type matters for ordering. A
.I number
sort key orders 2, 9, 10, 100; the same values under a
.I string
key order 10 before 9. Declare what the values are.
.PP
Without a sort key, items can only be read one at a time by
.BR euclid-cli-ekv-get-item (1)
or enumerated by
.BR euclid-cli-ekv-scan (1).
With one, a partition can be read as a range by
.BR euclid-cli-ekv-query (1),
which is the reason to have one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fITABLE\fR
Table name, unique within the account. Required.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-partition\-key " " \fIATTRIBUTE\fR
The attribute every item is identified by. Required.
.TP
.BR \-\-partition\-key\-type " " \fITYPE\fR
Its type: \fIstring\fR, \fInumber\fR or \fIbinary\fR. Defaults to
\fIstring\fR.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-sort\-key " " \fIATTRIBUTE\fR
The attribute items within a partition are ordered by. Optional, and
has to be a different attribute from the partition key.
.TP
.BR \-\-sort\-key\-type " " \fITYPE\fR
Its type: \fIstring\fR, \fInumber\fR or \fIbinary\fR. Defaults to
\fIstring\fR. Ignored when there is no sort key.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The table was created; its description is printed.
.TP
.B 1
A table of that name exists already, a key attribute was empty, started
with \fI$\fR or contained \fI.\fR, the two keys named the same
attribute, or a type was none of the three.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
# One record per supplier, read by id
euclid-cli ekv create-table --name suppliers --partition-key supplierId

# Many deliveries per supplier, in the order they arrived
euclid-cli ekv create-table --name deliveries \e
    --partition-key supplierId --sort-key deliveredAt

# Versions of a document, ordered as numbers rather than as text
euclid-cli ekv create-table --name versions \e
    --partition-key docId --sort-key version --sort-key-type number
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ekv (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekv-describe-table (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekv-delete-table (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekv-put-item (1)
